  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Find the sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of the geometric series \n\n$$\n1.5+1.2+0.96+0.768+\u22ef.\n$$\n\nDo not round the answer.\n\n${S}_{\\infty }=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of a geometric series is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{\\infty }=\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r},\\,|r|<1,\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nFor the given geometric series, the first term is ${a}_{1}=1.5$ and the common ratio is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{1.2}{1.5}=0.8.\n$$\n\nSo, using the formula, we find that the sum to infinity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{\\infty } & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.5}{1-0.8} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.5}{0.2} \\\\  & =7.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
